 "notes": "Gaffney-Kings Mountain folio (Keith and Sterrett, 1931), packet 1 (pages 1-7). Pages 1-26 are a scanned copy of the folio text (2428_t.pdf) whose descriptive part repeats the cleaner text.pdf copy on pages 27-39 word for word; pages 1-3 are the standard Geologic Atlas explanation. To avoid double-counting, values are recorded once, from pages 27-42. Nothing recorded from this packet. SUBSURFACE: none.\nGaffney-Kings Mountain folio, packet 2 (pages 8-13). Pages 1-26 are a scanned copy of the folio text (2428_t.pdf) whose descriptive part repeats the cleaner text.pdf copy on pages 27-39 word for word; pages 1-3 are the standard Geologic Atlas explanation. To avoid double-counting, values are recorded once, from pages 27-42. Nothing recorded from this packet. SUBSURFACE: none.\nGaffney-Kings Mountain folio, packet 3 (pages 14-28). Pages 14-26: Pages 1-26 are a scanned copy of the folio text (2428_t.pdf) whose descriptive part repeats the cleaner text.pdf copy on pages 27-39 word for word; pages 1-3 are the standard Geologic Atlas explanation. To avoid double-counting, values are recorded once, from pages 27-42. Pages 27-28 (text.pdf) give location, geography, relief and drainage (altitudes 430 to 1,705 ft), none of which fits the schema. Nothing recorded from this packet. SUBSURFACE: none.\nGaffney-Kings Mountain folio, packet 4 (pages 29-34): formations from the generalized columnar sections (figs. 2 and 3) and the order-of-formations table on page 29, and thrust faulting (page 33). About two-thirds of the district is in South Carolina (Cherokee and York Counties); the formations cross the state line and are recorded for the district. Archean symbols printed as A with a superscript are OCR'd as 'XR' and flagged inferred. Detailed formation descriptions (pages 30-32), local structure (page 33) and mineral resources (page 34) not itemized beyond this. SUBSURFACE: none.\nGaffney-Kings Mountain folio, packet 5 (pages 35-42): pages 35-39 mineral resources (iron ores, building stone, limestone, tin, monazite, graphite, water) not itemized as they do not fit the schema; pages 40-42 are the Gaffney areal and economic geology sheets and part of the Kings Mountain sheets, whose explanations repeat the formations recorded from page 29; only members and facies not named there are recorded from the page 40 explanation (OCR). SUBSURFACE: none.",
